	"nodes":[
		{"id":"e26c26cd25ef8ca2","type":"text","text":"- [ ] add Sara's job, at least that she has one. ","x":880,"y":-820,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"cd1c1f5e6cb9ba13","type":"text","text":"Maybe something like Sara \"I don't know if that's what I want.\"\n\nDon chuckled, \"that's what dating is for. Get to know her, see what you think of her.\" \n\nBasically Sara being unsure if she wants a relationship with Jane, and not being sure if she wants something long term, but Don's like that's no reason to hesitate, give it a try and see how it goes, and that's why Sara goes for it and is forward about her feelings with Jane. And Jane likes forward. \n\n----\n\n\"You like her right?\" Don asked. \n\n\"Well, yeah, she's just so... passionate.\" Sara smiled. She didn't know how else to put it, Jane was so wonderfully quirky. \n\n\"Then ask her out.\" Don was matter of fact about it.\n\nSara looked down. \"But what if... what if it can't work?\" \n\n\"Like what if you can't agree about the dishes or having kids or she snores like a train and you can't stand it?\" Don raised an eye brow. \n\nSara tried to keep her expression the same; Don had no way to know how squarely he'd hit the nail on the head with that middle one. \"Yeah, stuff like that.\" What if kids were a deal breaker for Jane? \n\nDon chuckled and smirked, \"That's what dating is for. So you can get to know her, she can get to know you. Figure all that stuff out.\" \n\nSara bit her lip, she was new to all of this. ","x":-460,"y":-1260,"width":590,"height":640},
		{"id":"af96d60070c46f08","type":"text","text":"As Jane and Sara are dating, at some point things are getting serious, and so Sara knows she needs to talk to Jane about something rather important. This might be before they become sexually active together, or at least shortly after they do. Definitely before Sara proposes and they get married (and they get married before Sara does eventually get pregnant so this conversation happens a long while before that). \n\nThey were on the couch, Sara holding Jane. Jane looked into her eyes, \"We could move to the bed? If you're ready for that?\" \n\nOh how Sara wanted that. But... there hadn't been a good time to tell Jane yet. \n\nWhen Sara hesitated, Jane touched her, \"No pressure, we can wait if you want to. Promise I don't mind.\"\n\n\"It's not that I don't want to.\" Sara kissed her, \"I've been fantasizing about this for a while now. About how would take you.\" Sara's voice was husky and rough, so she tried to take a deep breath and get it back to normal, \"But if we're going to do that, there's some things you should know first.\" \n\nJane was both excited and hesitant. Sara has fantasized about her? About them? Oh, how good that felt to know. And yet clearly this mattered to Sara. \"Things like what?\" There were too many possibilities that entered Jane's mind to make any type of guess. \n\nSara swallowed. \"Years ago,\" This was hard to talk about, \"back when I was still a teen,\" but Jane deserved to know, \"it's a long story, but the bottom line is,\" she wanted Jane to know, \"a doctor examined me and told me I'm likely infertile. That I'd probably never get pregnant or have kids of my own.\" Sara found that it helped to look at this as protecting Jane from not knowing. \"And that was before my training got... serious. The intense workouts come with side effects. One that's really common is that my cycles are irregular. Which makes pregnancy unlikely even for people that don't have other fertility issues. I just...\" Sara paused, \"I don't know if kids are a deal breaker for you.\" It hurt to say, but it was better to rip off the bandaid now before they got physically involved. Before things got even more serious between them, because then it would hurt even more. True, Jane hadn't really talked about babies, but Sara couldn't have them, and now Jane knew that. Sara tried to just wait as Jane thought. It was hard to wait, but it helped reminding herself that she had had years to think about this, and it made sense that Jane might need a few moments. It wasn't a small thing. \n\nJane was quiet as she turned it over in her mind. There was not one but different things that made pregnancy unlikely for Sara. The things was, did that bother Jane? Were children a deal breaker for her? She loved Sara, she knew that. But how did she feel about being with Sara knowing they might not have a family? But wait, that wasn't the only way. \"Well, what do you think about adopting?\" Jane realized that she did want a family. With Sara, one way or another. As long as Sara was ok with it. \n\nSara hadn't considered that, because she hadn't expected to find a lover at all. Sara really wished they could have children of their own, but given that they couldn't, she supposed at least then that would have family. So she nodded. \"Yeah, we could look into that. Some day.\"\n\nJane felt warm relief at being on the same page about this. \"Yeah, later on. When we have a bigger house.\"\n\n\"And more money.\" Sara said. Her paychecks right now weren't much, not yet anyway. But in time, they would get established, build careers, and then maybe a family. Not biological children, but Jane was right, they could at least look into adoption. \n\n\"When we're ready, we can figure it out.\" Jane leaned in for a kiss, and found Sara met her lips with deep passion. They would have a family one way or another when they were ready. In the mean time, Jane couldn't keep her hand off Sara. When she came up for air from all the kissing, \"Now, about those fantasies,\" she looked deep into Sara's eyes. ","x":240,"y":-1020,"width":480,"height":560},
		{"id":"e6b6718f6cb065d2","x":292,"y":-319,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"At first, Jane wanted to use a birth control option. They use a barrier method for a while. Sara had already experimented with hormonal birth control in the past, but instead of the performance stabilization many other female athletes saw, it caused major issues for her. Including interfering with weight management, making it impossible at times for her to choose what weight class she completed in. Thankfully, Jane had been so understanding about that part. \"It's fine, not everyone can do hormonal birth control. It's your body, it's up to you.\" She'd said. Sara had smiled, happy to have Jane in her corner. It was something she grew to really enjoy about their relationship: how much Jane loved her just as she was. Not that Sara would want Jane to change, but it made Sara happy that the feeling was mutual. It was so common that people expected Sara to be something other than what she was, it was why she had acted out some much as a teen. Sara had made peace with how she didn't fit society's norms, but it was still refreshing to have someone in her life who loved her exactly how she was. \n\nThough once they were married, Sara really didn't see the point. One time, that barrier method was giving them trouble, and Sara couldn't help but point out, \"You know, that really isn't necessary. I'm fine if we don't use it.\" \n\nJane looked at her, \"Really? You sure?\" \n\nUnfortunately Sara was sure it redundant, \"Yeah,\" it wasn't like she would get pregnant either way. The thought made kind of sad and hurt. To cover those feelings, she pulled Jane close and whispered in her ear, \"I'm sure I want to touch you.\" When Jane moaned in response, Sara kissed her neck. "}
	],
	"edges":[]
}